Z||000015||thomas_l||11-24-2001||08:35 AM||||I normally have room for three in mine. The "two-car" garage is actually one end of a full basement and goes all the way to the back of the house so it's like 1.5 regular cars deep (Maybe 2 Fieros would fit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). Normally I put my 87 GT in the front and use a floor jack to turn it sideways against the back wall. Then my truck (Chevy 1500 ex-cab short bed) will fit in behind it with 3-4 feet to spare with the door shut. The other side has my air compressor, tools, yard equip, etc. with enough room for my wife's C240.<P>This week, the garage has been taken over for a body/paint project on my 94 Crown Vic. The Fiero was moved to the backyard, my wife's car gets the extra space when the other isn't being worked on and my truck is in the driveway.||||reg||1
